From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:54:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] media: apple: avd: h264: complete the request and drop
 the job on early errors

avd_h264_run() leaves through err_free_jobs when growing the slice table
fails or when the slice buffer cannot be allocated. That path returns
before avd_run_postamble(), so the media request of the rejected slice is
never completed and every later request on the context fails with EBUSY.
It also frees ctx->job.segments without clearing the pointer: the next
slice of the same frame passes the !ctx->job.segments check, is written
into the freed table by stream_slice(), and avd_submit_job() frees it a
second time.

Complete the request on that path too, and set ctx->job.segments to
NULL after freeing it, so the rest of the frame is refused (-EINVAL) and
the next frame starts a new job.

The 7.1 version of this patch also reset slice_num in avd_h264_done();
7.2 does that itself.

Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 avd-h264.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/avd-h264.c b/avd-h264.c
index edb5280..5fcb251 100644
--- a/avd-h264.c
+++ b/avd-h264.c
@@ -829,7 +829,15 @@ static int avd_h264_run(struct avd_ctx *ctx)
 	return avd_submit_job(ctx);
 
 err_free_jobs:
+	/*
+	 * Complete the request (later requests on the context fail with EBUSY
+	 * otherwise) and drop the frame's job: the remaining slices of this
+	 * frame are refused by the !ctx->job.segments check until the next
+	 * frame starts a new job.
+	 */
+	avd_run_postamble(ctx, &run.base);
 	kvfree(ctx->job.segments);
+	ctx->job.segments = NULL;
 	return ret;
 }
 
